# VDR Directory Design

## Company and Users

VDR is a fictional 15-person company with 10 IT employees,
3 Finance employees, 1 HR employee, and 1 owner.

The owner's lab account is separate from my administrator
account, even though both display the name Nikhil Midde.

I created five users manually, nine through CSV import,
and Reese Clark manually afterward.

## Group Design

All groups are Security groups with Assigned membership.

| Group | Members | Owner | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|---|
| SEC-Dept-IT | 10 | Jordan Lee | Organize IT employees |
| SEC-Dept-Finance | 3 | Morgan Chen | Organize Finance employees |
| SEC-Dept-HR | 1 | Nikhil Midde | Organize the HR function |
| SEC-Role-Leadership | 3 | Nikhil Midde | Organize the owner and department managers |
| SEC-Role-Helpdesk | 2 | Jordan Lee | Organize Casey and Taylor's support responsibilities |

Department groups represent where people work. Role groups
represent responsibilities that may overlap departments.

HR currently has one member. I kept a department group so
future HR employees can join the same structure.

Group descriptions identify who approves membership changes.
They document a process; they do not enforce an approval workflow.

## Access and Ownership

Group owners manage membership. Members are the people who
would receive access if resources were assigned to the group.

Creating these groups did not grant application access or
Entra administrator roles. Job titles also grant no permissions.

## Contractors

This version of VDR contains employees only and differs from
the handout's contractor scenario.

Before adding contractors, I would document their sponsor,
contract end date, approved access, and offboarding process.
They would not automatically inherit employee department access.

## Problems and Fixes

The bulk import failed because initial passwords contained
usernames. I reviewed the operation results, changed the
passwords privately, and successfully retried the import.

The CSV contained nine users rather than ten. I added Reese
manually to reach 15 company users.

I corrected inconsistent department spelling before importing.
Passwords will be replaced with placeholders in the public CSV.

## Scaling to 500 People

I would document account naming and duplicate-name handling,
standardize department values, automate provisioning, and
establish membership reviews and contractor offboarding.

Department-only access would become insufficient when people
need different access within the same team. Role and resource
requirements would need separate review.

I would consider dynamic membership with appropriate licensing
and export audit logs for longer retention. These improvements
have not been implemented in this lab.

